V3DRender 0.09: kit 11, the buffer area's size
===============================================

Mesa draws through V3DRender (riscos-mesa's test 5, all passed).
0.09 makes the buffer area's size settable; it was always 1 GB of
address space. It's now 256 MB unless you say otherwise:

  *RMLoad V3DRender Size 512      (16 to 2048 MB)
  *Set V3DRender$Size 512         (in !Boot, before V3DRender loads)

It's address space only: memory is taken as GPU buffers are made and
given back when they're freed. All the GPU's buffers at any one time
must fit in it. *V3DRender shows the size as "Buffer memory".

Check runs every earlier test (1-8, all passed in kit 5) on 0.09;
Replay still replays Mesa's old job (it should hang in the same
runs as kit 10, and finish in the others).

Before you start
- A Pi 4, Pi 400 or CM4 with RISC OS 5.30 or later. V3DDriver not
  loaded. Copy this folder to a hard disc.

The test
1. Double-click Replay. It loads V3DRender 0.09 from this folder, in
   place of an older one. No program should be using the GPU at the same time:
   Replay needs the buffer addresses Mesa's job had.
2. Optional: double-click Check too (kits 1-5's tests, all passed in
   kit 5).
3. Send Results back.
